/C [1.0 0.819611 0.0]
/Contents <>
/CreationDate (D:20161007083519+01'00')
/F 28
/M (D:20161007083529+01'00')
/NM (0c062f39-4be9-47b5-81b7-9c06640c3421)
/Name /Comment
/P 37 0 R
/Popup 594 0 R
/RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:15.17.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:12.0pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:+6.0pt;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">3</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">Exercise therapy &#13;</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Eleven of the individual papers included in these reviews \(all RCTs, N = 536\) evaluated the efficacy of an exercise therapy intervention for the primary outcome of self-reported function \(Oostendorp 1987, Wester, Jespersen et al. 1996, Hoiness, Engebretsen et al. 2003, Clark and Burden 2005, Bassett and Prapavessis 2007, Bleakley, O'Connor et al. 2007, Hale, Hertel et al. 2007, van Rijn, van Os et al. 2007, van Rijn, van Heest et al. 2009, Hultman, Faltstrm et al. 2010\). Eight of these eleven studies reported a positive outcome for self-reported function following an exercise therapy intervention \(Oostendorp 1987, Wester, Jespersen et al. 1996, Clark and Burden 2005, Bleakley, O'Connor et al. 2007, Hale, Hertel et al. 2007, van Rijn, van Heest et al. 2009, Hultman, Faltstrm et al. 2010\), with three reporting no effect \(Hoiness, Engebretsen et al. 2003, Bassett and Prapavessis 2007, van Rijn, van Os et al. 2007\). The length of follow-up varied considerably in these reports, ranging from between 2-weeks \(Bassett and Prapavessis 2007\) and 8-months \(Wester, Jespersen et al. 1996\).&#13;</span></p></body>)
/Rect [323.337 225.555 341.337 243.555]
/Subj (Sticky Note)
/Subtype /Text
/T (Cailbhe)
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
