/Parent 595 0 R
/Rect [595.276 81.9662 775.276 201.966]
/Subtype /Popup
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
597 0 obj
<<
/AP <<
/N 1209 0 R
>>
/C [1.0 0.819611 0.0]
/Contents <>
/CreationDate (D:20161007083811+01'00')
/F 28
/M (D:20161007083817+01'00')
/NM (852ba4f2-3958-4dd1-8cc4-082171a894f2)
/Name /Comment
/P 37 0 R
/Popup 598 0 R
/RC (<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:15.17.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:12.0pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:+6.0pt;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">5</span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">Five of the reviews made specific conclusions regarding the secondary outcomes of proprioception \(Baltaci and Kohl 2003, Zoch, Fialka-Moser et al. 2003, Zech, Hubscher et al. 2009, Postle, Pak et al. 2012\), strength \(Zoch, Fialka-Moser et al. 2003, Zech, Hubscher et al. 2009, Feger, Herb et al. 2015\), muscle activity \(Zech, Hubscher et al. 2009\) and performance \(static/dynamic postural control\)\(Zech, Hubscher et al. 2009, Postle, Pak et al. 2012\). Their conclusions were discrepant however in that some reported that the exercise therapy intervention coincided with improvements in these secondary outcomes \(quality = 2/11 \(Baltaci and Kohl 2003\); 6/11 \(Feger, Herb et al. 2015\); 5/11 \(Zoch, Fialka-Moser et al. 2003\)\) while others concluded that no change had occurred \(quality = 8 \(Postle, Pak et al. 2012\); 9/11\(Zech, Hubscher et al. 2009\)\). Of the forty-one individual reports which assessed the efficacy of an exercise therapy intervention for ankle sprain, twenty \(14 RCTs, 6 non-RCTs; N = 710\) evaluated at least one of the secondary outcomes of proprioception, strength, muscle activity and/or static/dynamic postural control \(Freeman 1965, Tropp, Ekstrand et al. 1984, Forkin, Koczur et al. 1996, Bernier and Perrin 1998, Holme, Magnusson et al. 1999, Uh, Beynnon et al. 2000, Eils and Rosenbaum 2001, Hess, Joyce et al. 2001, Matsusaka, Yokoyama et al. 2001, Osborne, Chou et al. 2001, Hoiness, Engebretsen et al. 2003, Kaminski, Buckley et al. 2003, Powers, Buckley et al. 2004, Chaiwanichsiri, Lorprayoon et al. 2005, Clark and Burden 2005, Ross and Guskiewicz 2006, Hale, Hertel et al. 2007, Kidgell, Horvath et al. 2007, Ross 2007, Han, Ricard et al. 2009\). &#13;Five of these reported on the secondary outcome of proprioception \(Freeman, Dean et al. 1965, Tropp, Ekstrand et al. 1984, Forkin, Koczur et al. 1996, Bernier and Perrin 1998, Eils and Rosenbaum 2001\), three of which reported improvements following an exercise therapy intervention \(Freeman, Dean et al. 1965, Forkin, Koczur et al. 1996, Eils and Rosenbaum 2001\) and with the remaining 2 reporting no effect \(Tropp, Ekstrand et al. 1984, Bernier and Perrin 1998\). Five studies \(Holme, Magnusson et al. 1999, Uh, Beynnon et al. 2000, Hoiness, Engebretsen et al. 2003, Kaminski, Buckley et al. 2003, Powers, Buckley et al. 2004\) evaluated the effectiveness of exercise therapy on strength following acute ankle sprain, with only one of these \(Uh, Beynnon et al. 2000\) reporting any improvements. Muscle reaction times \(onset latency\) were considered to improve in all cases following an exercise therapy intervention \(Eils and Rosenbaum 2001, Osborne, Chou et al. 2001, Clark and Burden 2005\). Of the twelve studies that evaluated static/dynamic postural control, six \(Eils and Rosenbaum 2001, Chaiwanichsiri, Lorprayoon et al. 2005, Ross and Guskiewicz 2006, Hale, Hertel et al. 2007, Kidgell, Horvath et al. 2007, Han, Ricard et al. 2009\) reported a positive effect of an exercise therapy intervention while six \(Holme, Magnusson et al. 1999, Hess, Joyce et al. 2001, Matsusaka, Yokoyama et al. 2001, Hoiness, Glott et al. 2003, Powers, Buckley et al. 2004, Ross 2006\) reported no effect. Two studies evaluated the effect of exercise therapy on ROM with one reporting no effect \(van Rijn, van Os et al. 2007\) and the other reporting a positive effect \(Youdas, McLean et al. 2008\).&#13; None of the reviews made any specific conclusions for the secondary outcome of ROM. </span><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#A5A5A5;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal">&#13;</span></p></body>)
/Rect [412.401 165.556 430.401 183.556]
/Subj (Sticky Note)
/Subtype /Text
/T (Cailbhe)
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
